# Shipped with OpenXS (not user-editable config) - general exploit-kit
# signatures worth detecting on every install, not just this fleet's own
# accounts. Ships via git pull + install.sh, always loaded in addition
# to the local, per-server /etc/openxs/rules. Same relationship to that
# file as default_ignore has to /etc/openxs/ignore.
#
# "Self-doubled MD5" password-gated backdoor: md5($x.md5($x))==(hash),
# then some gated payload (eval, base64_decode, file_put_contents, an
# SSRF/outbound-request relay, ...). Found live 2026-10-24: 13 of these
# were already caught by generic YARA heuristics (ObfuscatedPhp etc.),
# but 5 variants of the exact same kit used a plain, unobfuscated hash
# literal with an SSRF-relay payload instead of eval/file_put_contents -
# none of our existing rules key on dangerous-sink keywords that happen
# to not be present in that variant, so those 5 went completely
# undetected. This regex targets the one structural element present in
# every variant regardless of payload: the self-doubled MD5 gate itself.
md5\(\s*\$\w+(\[[^\]]+\])?\s*\.\s*md5\(\s*\$\w+(\[[^\]]+\])?\s*\)\s*\)\s*==\s*\(
